WEBVTT

00:00:39.914 --> 00:00:42.499
Hey, easy there, Berger.
What do you think you're doing?

00:00:42.667 --> 00:00:44.418
- What?
- They're Helljumpers.

00:00:44.586 --> 00:00:47.421
Every one of those guys
are ODSTs from the 105th.

00:00:47.797 --> 00:00:50.632
They're in a whole different league.
Let's go.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:52.509
Unh. Aw, come on.

00:00:52.677 --> 00:00:53.677
I wanna hear what they're saying.

00:00:53.845 --> 00:00:55.304
No.

00:00:55.472 --> 00:00:57.556
I don't get it.

00:00:57.891 --> 00:00:59.808
How did everybody conveniently forget...

00:00:59.976 --> 00:01:02.186
...that I'm the best shot
this side of Eridanus?

00:01:02.353 --> 00:01:05.481
Getting assigned to backup
is a bunch of B.S.

00:01:05.648 --> 00:01:08.776
Contingency. It's an important mission.

00:01:08.943 --> 00:01:11.570
If the first sniper misses,
they take the shot.

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:13.489
I don't miss. I never miss.

00:01:13.656 --> 00:01:15.699
This sucks and you know it.

00:01:15.867 --> 00:01:17.576
I'm nobody's babysitter.

00:01:17.786 --> 00:01:20.788
Especially not some
farm-boy moose hunter.

00:01:20.955 --> 00:01:23.040
I hate to be the one
to break the bad news...

00:01:23.208 --> 00:01:26.460
...but you weren't selected to be
the primary shooter on this mission.

00:01:26.628 --> 00:01:30.464
So it seems
they want your farm boy to do it.

00:01:30.632 --> 00:01:33.759
I guess that makes you the backup.
Sorry, O'Brian.

00:01:34.677 --> 00:01:35.761
I'm the backup?

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:40.766
- And the shooter is a Spartan.
- What?

00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:44.853
And that means
this mission just got escalated.

00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:01.078
This is Spartan Cal-141...

00:02:01.246 --> 00:02:03.789
...who'll be the ranking officer
on this mission.

00:02:03.957 --> 00:02:05.707
I realize that is highly unusual...

00:02:05.875 --> 00:02:08.794
...and you have strong feelings
about Spartans.

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:13.590
You will keep those feelings
out of the mission and follow the plan.

00:02:14.843 --> 00:02:17.553
Satellite recon shows radar
and magnetic signatures...

00:02:17.720 --> 00:02:19.888
...on high end in the Arc star cluster.

00:02:20.056 --> 00:02:22.599
These signatures indicate
a complex of buildings.

00:02:22.767 --> 00:02:24.268
It's a logistical base.

00:02:24.435 --> 00:02:28.021
The Prophet you are targeting
is in control of this entire sector.

00:02:28.231 --> 00:02:31.775
Our mission is simple.
We want this Prophet dead.

00:02:31.943 --> 00:02:36.280
We take out the Prophet, we will
stop the Covenant chain of supply.

00:02:37.031 --> 00:02:38.949
If we achieve the goal of this mission...

00:02:39.117 --> 00:02:42.286
...we will able to buy ourselves months
of tactical advantage.

00:02:42.996 --> 00:02:47.291
And we will do all of this
with minimal risk to the UNSC.

00:02:47.709 --> 00:02:51.295
Hmm.
Other than to this group, of course.

00:02:51.588 --> 00:02:56.508
Cortez, fill them in on the details.

00:02:57.385 --> 00:03:01.680
Right. You'll be flying into the atmosphere
with a Leonid-class meteor shower.

00:03:01.848 --> 00:03:04.808
Meteor showers
are a regular occurrence on this planet...

00:03:04.976 --> 00:03:07.978
...so that means entry and landing
should go unnoticed.

00:03:08.146 --> 00:03:11.690
Calculations show reaching the target
will take a 14-hour fast march...

00:03:11.858 --> 00:03:13.233
...from your entry point.

00:03:13.610 --> 00:03:14.902
Once you reach the target...

00:03:15.069 --> 00:03:17.779
...take out the Prophet
as soon as he steps off that ship.

00:03:18.281 --> 00:03:22.993
Then you are to gather all data
relating to the unidentified alien ruins.

00:03:23.161 --> 00:03:25.621
What do you mean,
they're not identified?

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:27.664
The architecture is
not Covenant-designed...

00:03:27.832 --> 00:03:29.833
...and it sure as hell
wasn't built by humans.

00:03:30.001 --> 00:03:32.002
They predate both sides.

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:34.630
This site is of the utmost importance.

00:03:34.839 --> 00:03:37.007
We photograph everything.

00:03:37.217 --> 00:03:39.635
That will be all, master sergeant.
Rejoin your men.

00:03:40.011 --> 00:03:42.429
You will be dropping
in precisely five minutes.

00:03:42.597 --> 00:03:45.641
With this mission,
there is no room for delay or error.

00:03:46.184 --> 00:03:49.144
Good luck, and Godspeed.

00:05:24.324 --> 00:05:25.991
Dutch, come in.

00:05:26.159 --> 00:05:28.535
I'm all right. Where's O'Brian?

00:05:33.207 --> 00:05:34.958
Over there.

00:05:49.265 --> 00:05:51.183
His oxygen tank.

00:05:51.684 --> 00:05:53.310
Dutch, get the gear.

00:05:53.478 --> 00:05:55.187
We gotta get him out of there.

00:06:36.396 --> 00:06:40.023
Are you guys nuts? Why are you
throwing me around like that?

00:06:51.619 --> 00:06:53.578
We lost Checkman in the atmosphere.

00:06:53.746 --> 00:06:57.332
- What?
- And we almost lost you too.

00:07:09.887 --> 00:07:13.181
Their logistics and
refueling base is here. We're here.

00:07:14.058 --> 00:07:17.644
The Prophet will be coming in
at exactly 0800.

00:07:17.854 --> 00:07:22.399
Hmm. Everything depends on us
getting a clear shot from this location...

00:07:22.567 --> 00:07:25.944
...and we've got to hit him
as soon as he's exiting that ship.

00:07:26.112 --> 00:07:27.737
It's two miles from the target...

00:07:27.905 --> 00:07:30.574
...and should give us the elevation
for the shot.

00:07:30.741 --> 00:07:32.534
It's pretty far...

00:07:32.702 --> 00:07:35.996
...but it will give us enough cover
to make our extraction.

00:07:36.164 --> 00:07:39.916
Assuming that the Spartan
can make the shot, that is.

00:07:43.629 --> 00:07:45.797
And if we don't
make it to the target in time?

00:07:45.965 --> 00:07:47.757
There won't be any second chances.

00:07:47.925 --> 00:07:51.720
- It's a long-ass march.
- Then we better get marching.

00:08:16.120 --> 00:08:18.121
Wanna take the lens cap off?

00:08:18.289 --> 00:08:20.332
Knock it off, O'Brian.

00:11:08.167 --> 00:11:11.336
I'm not crippled. Put me down.

00:11:21.347 --> 00:11:22.555
You bitch any louder...

00:11:22.765 --> 00:11:24.974
...and this place will be crawling
with Covenant.

00:11:25.142 --> 00:11:27.936
Shut your mouth! He just got lucky.

00:11:44.370 --> 00:11:46.371
That's twice.

00:11:46.789 --> 00:11:49.332
Twice he had to save your dumb ass
already.

00:11:49.500 --> 00:11:51.376
You could at least say "thank you."

00:12:02.012 --> 00:12:05.140
Man, those are some stairs.

00:12:52.772 --> 00:12:55.023
The shuttle will be
touching down in two minutes.

00:13:00.863 --> 00:13:04.574
After all this, he better
be everything they said he was.

00:14:09.849 --> 00:14:11.641
Take him out!

00:14:41.922 --> 00:14:44.799
Take the shot. O'Brian, now!

00:14:45.259 --> 00:14:48.177
You're the only one who can do it.

00:15:35.225 --> 00:15:37.727
It's the data on the ruins.

00:15:39.980 --> 00:15:41.731
Tell them...

00:15:42.942 --> 00:15:45.151
...to get it to Halsey.

00:15:45.945 --> 00:15:47.820
She'll know.

00:15:48.948 --> 00:15:50.448
No, you give it to her.

00:15:53.077 --> 00:15:58.206
We both know
that's not gonna be possible.

00:16:39.707 --> 00:16:41.541
Heard about what you guys did
down there.

00:16:41.750 --> 00:16:42.750
Took out a Prophet...

00:16:42.918 --> 00:16:45.920
...and stopped the Covenant's
supply chain dead for the sector.

00:16:46.338 --> 00:16:48.089
They say a Spartan died there.

00:16:48.257 --> 00:16:50.883
Went down faster than a new bood
on his first day.

00:16:51.051 --> 00:16:54.429
I thought those guys
were supposed to be unbeatable.

00:16:54.972 --> 00:16:59.517
Huh. I guess he didn't have what it takes
to hang with the Helljumpers, huh?

00:16:59.685 --> 00:17:01.060
Shut up.

00:17:03.772 --> 00:17:06.107
What's your problem?
What is the matter with you?

00:17:06.275 --> 00:17:08.151
What'd I say?
